<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Commands on kevin</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/</link><description>Recent content in Commands on kevin</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>run</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/run/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/run/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-run"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-run"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Creates the environment&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt; steps in dependency order, then blocks until&#10;an interrupt. On Ctrl-C, &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt; removes the steps in reverse order.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin run&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin run --keep --open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Flag&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--keep&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;leave the environment in place on exit&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--open&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;open the console in the default browser once it&amp;rsquo;s listening&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/environment-file/"&gt;Configuring an environment&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for what an &lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt; step is.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>setup</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/setup/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/setup/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-setup"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin setup&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-setup"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Runs the environment&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; DAG. These steps persist across runs, such as&#10;a shared kind cluster reused by many &lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;s.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin setup&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin setup --open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Flag&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--open&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;open the console in the default browser once it&amp;rsquo;s listening&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/environment-file/"&gt;Configuring an environment&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for the difference between a &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; step and an &lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt; step.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>teardown</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/teardown/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/teardown/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-teardown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin teardown&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-teardown"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Runs the environment&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; DAG in reverse, removing what &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt;&#10;installed.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin teardown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>init</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/init/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/init/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-init"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin init&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-init"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Resolves each &lt;code&gt;plugins:&lt;/code&gt; entry a step actually uses, downloading and&#10;extracting a &lt;code&gt;file:&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;oci:&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;http:&lt;/code&gt; source and verifying its signature if&#10;&lt;code&gt;signed: true&lt;/code&gt; is set. It starts no plugin process and validates nothing&#10;against a schema.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prints the qualified name of every plugin it fetched, one per line.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>validate</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/validate/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/validate/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-validate"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin validate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-validate"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Loads the environment file, starts its declared plugins, and validates every&#10;step&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;with&lt;/code&gt; block against its plugin&amp;rsquo;s schema: everything &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt; and&#10;&lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; do before touching Docker. It creates nothing and needs no Docker&#10;daemon.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prints the project name and the setup/env step counts on success.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>plugin</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/plugin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/plugin/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-plugin"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin plugin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-plugin"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Works with the plugins that ship inside &lt;code&gt;kevin&lt;/code&gt;, and with the plugin&#10;package format used by &lt;code&gt;plugins:&lt;/code&gt; entries in &lt;code&gt;kevin.cue&lt;/code&gt; (see&#10;&lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/environment-file/"&gt;Configuring an environment&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="kevin-plugin-pack-dir"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin plugin pack &amp;lt;dir&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-plugin-pack-dir"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Builds a plugin package (a gzip-compressed tar) from &lt;code&gt;dir&lt;/code&gt;: a&#10;&lt;code&gt;manifest.json&lt;/code&gt; plus the entrypoint binary and any files it needs&#10;alongside it. &lt;code&gt;dir&lt;/code&gt; may already hold a &lt;code&gt;manifest.json&lt;/code&gt;; the override flags&#10;below fill in or replace its fields, and must fully supply the manifest&#10;when &lt;code&gt;dir&lt;/code&gt; has none.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ca</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/ca/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/ca/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-ca"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin ca&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-ca"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Manages the kevin root CA in the trust stores of this machine. It needs no&#10;project - the root names none and is shared by every kevin project on the&#10;machine. See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/ca-and-trust/"&gt;the CA and trust guide&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for the full picture.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="kevin-ca-install"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin ca install&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-ca-install"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generates the kevin root CA if it does not already exist, then adds it to&#10;the trust stores of this machine. Run this once for the machine; there is&#10;no need to repeat it per project.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>do</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/do/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/do/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-do-name----extra-args"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin do &amp;lt;name&amp;gt; [-- extra args...]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-do-name----extra-args"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Looks up &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; in the &lt;code&gt;kevin.cue&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;commands&lt;/code&gt; block, exports the environment&#10;of every step its &lt;code&gt;needs&lt;/code&gt; list names, and execs its &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt; argv in place of&#10;&lt;code&gt;kevin&lt;/code&gt; - the same mechanism &lt;code&gt;connect&lt;/code&gt; uses, with a predefined command&#10;instead of an ad-hoc one. Any args after &lt;code&gt;--&lt;/code&gt; append to the command&amp;rsquo;s own&#10;&lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt; argv.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>